{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== TRIAGE: the OUTBOUND transition-status cell — ROOT CAUSE PROVEN. It is a PRODUCT DEFECT,\nand 7f93 does NOT cover it. Filed as [rebar:d067-5d2f-bcee-46ae]. ===\n\nTHE OUTBOUND PATH NEVER CALLS `transition_issue_by_name`, so 7f93's fix to that method cannot\nreach it. 7f93 fixed the INBOUND cell because `_in_status` calls the transport method DIRECTLY.\nThe outbound cell goes somewhere else entirely, and that somewhere has no status handling on DC.\n\nTHE CHAIN, read end to end and cited:\n 1. `adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py:81-82` — the local `in_progress` becomes\n    `fields[\"status\"] = \"In Progress\"` via `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` (`value_maps.py:49-57`).\n 2. `dispatch_apply_phases.py:41` — `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST` CONTAINS `\"status\"`, so\n    `_update_one_filter_fields` (`:130-139`) KEEPS it rather than stripping it.\n 3. `dispatch_one.py:665` — `_update_one_scalar_update` forwards the whole allowlisted dict as\n    `client.update_issue(issue_key, **fields)`.\n 4. `applier.py:591` — that `client` is `_load_acli()`, which is\n    `select_backend(load_config()).transport` (`applier.py:221-231`). On this deployment,\n    `JiraDataCenterTransport`.\n 5. **THE FORK.** On Cloud, `adapters/jira/acli.py:170` POPS `status` out of the kwargs and\n    `:182-183` routes it to `transition_issue` -> `transition_issue_by_name`. The\n    status→transition translation lives IN THE TRANSPORT, once, per vendor.\n    On Data Center, `adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py:248-255` pops ONLY `assignee` and\n    puts everything else into `issue.update(fields=kwargs)` — a REST field EDIT. `status` is\n    not an editable Jira field; it is reachable only through a transition. Jira rejects it, the\n    failure is soft-failed, the pass exits 0, and `fields.status.name` stays `'To Do'`.\n\nSo the DC transport is MISSING a capability its Cloud sibling has. Same shape as bug 3f04\n(outbound links wired into one apply path only): a translation implemented per-transport, and\nthe second transport never got it.\n\nREPRODUCED WITHOUT LIVE JIRA — `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_outbound_status_routing_5200.py`:\n  * `test_the_dc_transport_edits_status_as_a_field_instead_of_transitioning` — GREEN today, pins\n    the mechanism: `update_issue(\"DIG-1\", status=\"In Progress\")` yields\n    `edited_fields == [{\"status\": \"In Progress\"}]`, `transitions_probed == []`,\n    `transitioned == []`. **No transitions probe happens at all**, which is the decisive\n    observation — it rules out \"the transition was attempted and rejected\".\n  * `test_an_outbound_status_should_dispatch_the_transition_that_reaches_it` —\n    `xfail(strict=True)`. Checked with `--runxfail` that it fails naming the PROPERTY, not an\n    AttributeError: `AssertionError: the outbound status 'In Progress' must resolve to\n    transition 'Start Progress' (id 11) and be dispatched; got transitioned=[] and\n    edited_fields=[{'status': 'In Progress'}]`. `strict=True` so the build breaks when the bug\n    is fixed and the marker cannot go stale.\n\nWHY IT WAS INVISIBLE ON CLOUD: the Cloud transport is ACLI-shaped and its `update_issue` is a\nCLI edit that could never carry a status, so the routing had to be written there. The DC\ntransport is REST-shaped and `issue.update(fields=...)` accepts an arbitrary field dict without\ncomplaint at the call site — the rejection happens server-side, one layer past where a reader\nlooks. Nothing about the DC code reads as missing.\n\nNO J11 TEST CHANGE IS NEEDED. `_out_status` drives `rebar.transition(local_id, current,\n\"in_progress\")` and `_oracle_out_status` asserts `fields.status.name == \"In Progress\"`. Both are\ncorrect; the cell is reporting a real bug. It stays red until d067 lands."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785691355874586001,"uuid":"e7025629-4409-4f8b-b42e-cf7c33769485"}